{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For in vain</b> — that the net not be seen, so that [the bird] not fear it, until it settles upon it; it sees the food that is in it and not the net. So they see what they will take and say: 'all precious wealth is found,' but they do not see the net, for they walk upon it, as stated: <i>for he sends a net against his feet</i>."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:45.336140461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}